WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
Managing traps and field programs across multiple sites can take a lot of time,

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.860
particularly when teams and equipment are spread over a large area.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.860
WildTrkr brings that information together in one place.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.200
Devices can be allocated to team members and organised into programs,

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.960
giving both field staff and managers a clear view of what is happening in the field.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.640
When a trap is activated, the appropriate team member receives an email alert and can open

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.720
WildTrkr to see exactly which device needs attention. From the map and list view,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.520
you can quickly see which traps are active, which have been triggered,

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.660
and whether any devices have missed a check-in and need to be checked in person.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:46.580
Field outcomes can be recorded as the work is completed, providing an ongoing record of

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:51.680
captures and other field activities. And because that information is already being collected,

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.680
reports can be generated without having to piece everything together afterwards.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.020
WildTrkr, Smarter Field Monitoring.

